:\"/supplier/spl_1JFA2B4TV1S0B6R3\",\"t\":\"CREW Carbon\"},{\"h\":\"https://350solutions.com\",\"t\":\"350Solutions\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/wastewater-alkalinity-enhancement/1.1\",\"t\":\"Wastewater Alkalinity Enhancement v1.1\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/wastewater-alkalinity-enhancement/1.0\",\"t\":\"Wastewater Alkalinity Enhancement v1.0\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JFA2B4TV1S0B6R3/prj_1JFA3YY9P1S0YVKR/pjd_1JT3PSC0W1S0VTM1/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"Project Design Document | 30 Apr 2025\"},{\"h\":\"/ghg-entry/rmv_1KY0AC0201S0EATR?tab=calculation-view\",\"t\":\"See GHG entry →\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JFA2B4TV1S0B6R3/prj_1JFA3YY9P1S0YVKR/pjd_1M0T6ZRYG1S0QAVC/verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JFA2B4TV1S0B6R3/prj_1JFA3YY9P1S0YVKR/pjd_1M0T6ZDAC1S0G142/ghg_statement_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JFA2B4TV1S0B6R3/prj_1JFA3YY9P1S0YVKR/pjd_1KWARX07R1S0WK2Y/verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JFA2B4TV1S0B6R3/prj_1JFA3YY9P1S0YVKR/pjd_1KWARB83R1S0PVN1/ghg_statement_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JFA2B4TV1S0B6R3/prj_1JFA3YY9P1S0YVKR/pjd_1KVGB39RX1S0104W/ghg_statement_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"VALIDATED\\nMARINE\\n1,000Y+\\nNew England WAE Project\\nCREW Carbon\\nISSUED\\n1,374.73\\nBUFFER POOL\\n27.504\\nCREDITING PERIOD\\n11 Jul 2023 to 10 Jul 2028\\nSummary\\nRemoval method\\nCalculation overview\\nProject documentation\\nCertificates\\nReversal risk\\nSummary\\n\\nCREW removes carbon dioxide from the atmosphere via wastewater treatment systems, deploying fine-grained natural minerals like calcium carbonate in wastewater treatment systems. The deployment locations for this project are municipal wastewater facilitiies that serve the New England area and discharge directly into the ocean. Onsite, the feedstock is transferred into CREW’s dosing systems, and is dosed into the wastewater treatment reactors as a slurry. CREW’s system controls the rate of dosing to optimize process benefits and CDR.\\n\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nCurrent verifier\\n350Solutions\\n->\\nProject code\\nX8KC\\nApproval date\\n30 Apr 2025\\nCurrent protocol version\\nWastewater Alkalinity Enhancement v1.1\\nBaseline protocol version\\nWastewater Alkalinity Enhancement v1.0\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nNew England WAE Project\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nMarine carbon dioxide removal (mCDR) leverages the ocean's natural capacity to absorb and store carbon for thousands of years. These pathways use the biogeochemical and physical properties of the ocean and other bodies of water to capture carbon dioxide from the atmosphere or to permanently store carbon already contained within them. Approaches to mCDR include Ocean Alkalinity Enhancement and Direct Ocean Capture and Storage.\\n\\nProject Design Document\\n30 Apr 2025\\nCalculation overview\\nCalculations demonstrating 50.68 tCO₂e removed from New England WAE Project on 30 Jun 2026\\nSee GHG entry →\\nNet CO₂e Removed\\n50.677 t\\nSequestrations\\n61.875 t\\n-\\nActivities\\n11.050 tCO₂e\\n-\\nUncertainty Discount\\n148 kg\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nView full screen\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n24 Aug 2026\\tVerification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n24 Aug 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n29 Jun 2026\\tVerification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n29 Jun 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n19 Jun 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 5 of 16\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nCertificates\\nIssued\\n1,374.73\\nRetired\\n280\\nBuffer pool\\n27.504\\nCrediting period\\n11 Jul 2023 to 10 Jul 2028\\nIssuances\\nRetirements\\nIssue date\\tIssued\\tBuffer pool\\tSupplier allocation\\n24 Aug 2026\\t196.33\\t3.928\\t192.402\\n29 Jun 2026\\t223.51\\t4.471\\t219.039\\n19 Jun 2026\\t99.65\\t1.993\\t97.657\\n05 Jun 2026\\t158.4\\t3.17\\t155.23\\n05 Jun 2026\\t219.92\\t4.399\\t215.521\\n18 Dec 2025\\t372.52\\t7.453\\t365.067\\n30 Apr 2025\\t20.12\\t0.403\\t19.717\\n30 Apr 2025\\t84.28\\t1.687\\t82.593\\nShowing 8 of 8\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nReversal risk\\n\\nThe risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as very low. This means that 2% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to CREW Carbon's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 27.504 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 28.495 certificates.\\n\\nCREW Carbon has no reversals to date.\\n\\nLearn more about reversal risk\"}"